00:17:30.633 --> 00:17:33.636
And then you apply VSEPR.

00:17:33.636 --> 00:17:36.873
So there's no lone
pairs around the carbon.

00:17:36.873 --> 00:17:40.510
That doesn't matter for
the shape around carbon.

00:17:40.510 --> 00:17:42.345
OK, that's really important.

00:17:42.345 --> 00:17:44.447
So I pick my central atom.

00:17:44.447 --> 00:17:48.418
So now I know there's
no lone pairs, no LP,

00:17:48.418 --> 00:17:50.653
because central atom.

00:17:50.653 --> 00:17:53.022
You know what I
mean, central atom.

00:17:56.592 --> 00:17:58.995
And then finally,
three, we're going

00:17:58.995 --> 00:18:02.799
to get linear because,
again, there's

00:18:02.799 --> 00:18:05.935
only two electron domains.

00:18:05.935 --> 00:18:07.537
There's going to
electron domains,

00:18:07.537 --> 00:18:10.506
and the only geometry really
that you can take in this case

00:18:10.506 --> 00:18:11.707
is linear.

00:18:11.707 --> 00:18:13.643
No lone pairs, two
electron domains.

00:18:13.643 --> 00:18:14.477
Good.

00:18:14.477 --> 00:18:17.280
And now you know it's
