00:19:38.294 --> 00:19:40.396
OK, so that's what
they're going to do.

00:19:40.396 --> 00:19:45.101
And that is called
trigonal planar.

00:19:45.101 --> 00:19:49.605
It has a name trigonal planar.

00:19:49.605 --> 00:19:54.510
So you know, it's kind of--

00:19:54.510 --> 00:19:56.312
planar.

00:19:56.312 --> 00:19:58.314
So it's kind of right,
but it's not quite right

00:19:58.314 --> 00:20:00.149
because I drew with
90 degree angles,

00:20:00.149 --> 00:20:01.784
and that's not what
they are going to do

00:20:01.784 --> 00:20:04.954
to maximize their spacing here.

00:20:04.954 --> 00:20:07.690
They're going to go
at angles like that.

00:20:07.690 --> 00:20:09.892
All right, they're
going to find 120.

00:20:09.892 --> 00:20:15.064
So if I have three electron
regions, here we go, then--

00:20:15.064 --> 00:20:16.232
now I had three--

00:20:16.232 --> 00:20:18.534
OK, so the electron
pair geometry.

00:20:18.534 --> 00:20:19.802
Why is this different?

00:20:19.802 --> 00:20:21.804
You will see in a minute.

00:20:21.804 --> 00:20:27.009
The electron pair geometry
covers BPs and LPs,

00:20:27.009 --> 00:20:30.580
but in this case,
there's only BPs.

00:20:30.580 --> 00:20:31.113
Fine.

00:20:31.113 --> 00:20:32.982
There's still only three.

00:20:32.982 --> 00:20:36.252
Right, and so it's
trigonal planar.

00:20:39.889 --> 00:20:43.326
Trigonal planar.

00:20:43.326 --> 00:20:46.395
And guess what, if
there is no LPs--

00:20:46.395 --> 00:20:49.198
OK, so the structure
that the molecule takes

00:20:49.198 --> 00:20:52.668
or those electron domains
takes is trigonal planar.

00:20:52.668 --> 00:20:55.571
The structure that the molecule
takes if there is no LPs

00:20:55.571 --> 00:20:57.006
is also trigonal planar.

00:20:59.575 --> 00:21:04.180
But now, the moment
we've been waiting for

00:21:04.180 --> 00:21:07.316
is what happens when
that's not true,

00:21:07.316 --> 00:21:09.151
and you've got a lone pair.

00:21:09.151 --> 00:21:11.020
So again, we're going
to do this by example.

00:21:14.757 --> 00:21:17.960
OK, and so my next
example is formaldehyde,

00:21:17.960 --> 00:21:23.833
which is something we love to
